      "content": "# Test Checklist\n\n## Functionality\n- [ ] FT-1: Users can successfully register new accounts and log in to the community forum, and their login status is maintained correctly.\n\n- [ ] FT-2: Registered users can create or edit their profiles, including personal introductions and hobbies, and the information will display correctly after being saved.\n\n- [ ] FT-3: Logged-in users can create new discussion threads in different discussion categories, including titles and content, and successfully publish them.\n\n- [ ] FT-4: Users can post replies to any discussion thread, and the replies will be displayed in the thread's reply list in real time.\n\n- [ ] FT-5: Users can like or vote on posts or replies made by other users, and the count of likes/votes is updated in real time.\n\n- [ ] FT-6: Users can use the keyword search function to find posts, and the search results accurately match the title and body content.\n\n- [ ] FT-7: Users can filter the post list by discussion category, displaying only posts from the selected category.\n\n- [ ] FT-8: The forum homepage or specific sections can display a list of the most active discussions, sorted by recent interaction frequency.\n\n- [ ] FT-9: Users can view their entire posting and reply history.\n\n- [ ] FT-10: When browsing posts, users can view the poster's public profile information.\n\n- [ ] FT-11: After a user edits a published post or reply, the page will display an \"Edited\" mark or the last edit time.\n\n- [ ] FT-12: The forum supports basic rich text editing features, such as bolding, links, and lists, and renders them correctly after posting.\n\n- [ ] FT-13: When a user logs out and logs back in, their profile, posting history, and interaction status are correctly restored.\n\n## Constraint\n- [ ] CS-14: When a user attempts to post a thread with an empty title or empty body, the system will block the submission and provide a warning.\n\n- [ ] CS-15: The system can prevent duplicate submissions of the same content (such as repeatedly and rapidly posting the same reply).\n\n## Content\n- [ ] CT-16: The forum homepage or specific sections can display a list of recently popular discussions, sorted by the number of likes, replies, or activity levels."
